  "specDocument": "## Rules\nR1: A `Track` must be created with a rating integer in the inclusive range 1‑5. The behavior for ratings outside this range is undefined (students may assume the precondition holds).\nR2: `InsertionOrderStrategy.order(Playlist)` returns a list containing the tracks of the given playlist in the exact order they were added (insertion order).\nR3: `RatingOrderStrategy.order(Playlist)` returns a list containing the same tracks sorted primarily by rating descending (higher rating first). For tracks with equal rating the relative order must be the same as in the original playlist (stable ordering).\nR4: `Player.getPlaybackOrder(Playlist)` returns the list produced by the currently configured `PlaybackStrategy`.\nR5: For an empty playlist all strategies return an empty list.\nR6: For a playlist containing a single track the returned list contains exactly that track.\nR7: No strategy may modify the internal order of the supplied `Playlist`.\n\n## Worked Examples\n| Rules | Input | Expected |\n|-------|-------|----------|\n| R2, R5, R6 | Playlist with one track **T** (rating 3). Strategy: `InsertionOrderStrategy`. | `[T]` |\n| R3, R5, R6 | Playlist with three tracks added in order: **A** (rating 3), **B** (rating 5), **C** (rating 5). Strategy: `RatingOrderStrategy`. | `[B, C, A]` (B and C keep insertion order because of equal rating) |\n\n## Design\n| Type | Role | Template status |\n|------|------|-----------------|\n| Track | Immutable data holder for a music track. | given |\n| Playlist | Holds tracks in insertion order and provides read‑only access. | given |\n| PlaybackStrategy | Interface defining `order(Playlist)` to produce a playback order. | student-creates |\n| InsertionOrderStrategy | Concrete `PlaybackStrategy` that returns tracks in insertion order. | student-creates |\n| RatingOrderStrategy | Concrete `PlaybackStrategy` that returns tracks sorted by rating descending, stable for ties. | student-creates |\n| Player | Holds a `PlaybackStrategy` and delegates `getPlaybackOrder(Playlist)` to it. | student-creates |\n\n## Public API\n### Track\n```java\npublic class Track {\n    public Track(String title, String artist, int rating, int durationSec) { ... }\n    public String getTitle();\n    public String getArtist();\n    public int getRating();\n    public int getDurationSec();\n}\n```\n### Playlist\n```java\npublic class Playlist {\n    public Playlist();\n    public void addTrack(Track track);\n    public java.util.List<Track> getTracks(); // returns tracks in insertion order\n}\n```\n### PlaybackStrategy\n```java\npublic interface PlaybackStrategy {\n    java.util.List<Track> order(Playlist playlist);\n}\n```\n### InsertionOrderStrategy\n```java\npublic class InsertionOrderStrategy implements PlaybackStrategy {\n    public InsertionOrderStrategy();\n    public java.util.List<Track> order(Playlist playlist);\n}\n```\n### RatingOrderStrategy\n```java\npublic class RatingOrderStrategy implements PlaybackStrategy {\n    public RatingOrderStrategy();\n    public java.util.List<Track> order(Playlist playlist);\n}\n```\n### Player\n```java\npublic class Player {\n    public Player(PlaybackStrategy strategy);\n    public void setStrategy(PlaybackStrategy strategy);\n    public PlaybackStrategy getStrategy();\n    public java.util.List<Track> getPlaybackOrder(Playlist playlist);\n}\n```\n\n## Testing Strategy\n| ID | Owner type | Observable responsibility | Weight | After‑due‑date |\n|----|------------|---------------------------|--------|----------------|\n| S1 | InsertionOrderStrategy | Returns tracks in insertion order (R2). Covers empty playlist and non‑empty playlist. | 3 | no |\n| S2 | RatingOrderStrategy | Returns tracks sorted by rating descending, stable for equal ratings (R3). Covers empty playlist, distinct ratings, and tie‑rating cases. | 3 | no |\n| S3 | Player | Delegates to the configured strategy and returns its result unchanged (R4). Tests with both `InsertionOrderStrategy` and `RatingOrderStrategy`, each on empty and non‑empty playlists. | 3 | no |\n\n## Contract Risk Inventory\n| Seam | Rules | Admitted partitions | Excluded inputs |\n|------|-------|---------------------|-----------------|\n| S1 | R2, R5 | S1.P1: empty playlist; S1.P2: playlist with ≥1 track | none |\n| S2 | R3, R5 | S2.P1: empty playlist; S2.P2: playlist where all ratings differ; S2.P3: playlist containing at least two tracks with equal rating | none |\n| S3 | R4, R5 | S3.P1: insertion strategy with empty playlist; S3.P2: insertion strategy with non‑empty playlist; S3.P3: rating strategy with empty playlist; S3.P4: rating strategy with non‑empty playlist | none |\n\n## Decision Ledger\n| Decision | Provenance | Why necessary | Observable |\n|----------|------------|----------------|------------|\n| Use `int` rating 1‑5 and precondition it (R1) | EXPLICIT_BRIEF | Rating range is part of the domain description. | Invalid ratings are undefined; tests only use 1‑5. |\n| Provide `getTracks()` returning insertion order | NECESSARY_OPERATIONAL_CHOICE | Strategies need read‑only access to the original order for stability. | Strategies receive same ordering as added. |\n| Define `PlaybackStrategy.order(Playlist)` returning a new `List<Track>` | NECESSARY_OPERATIONAL_CHOICE | Enables interchangeable strategies without mutating the playlist. | Returned list may be inspected without affecting playlist. |\n| Require stable sorting for equal ratings in `RatingOrderStrategy` | EXPLICIT_BRIEF | The brief explicitly states “ties keep insertion order”. | Order of equal‑rating tracks matches insertion order. |\n| Make `Player` mutable with `setStrategy` | PEDAGOGICAL_OBJECTIVE | Demonstrates the Strategy pattern’s ability to change behaviour at runtime. | Tests can switch strategies and observe changed output. |\n\n## Diagram\nyes – the design contains multiple collaborating types (`Player`, `PlaybackStrategy`, concrete strategies, `Playlist`, `Track`).\n",
